A||||1||Buster||Recent purchase help idle - LONG||||1||
Z||000000||Buster||08-05-2000||10:02 PM||||Purchased 88 V6 auto 78K in following running condition. Ran good warmed up at 40mph +. Poor idle and stumble when cold, somewhat better when warm but bad enough that I would not pull into traffic. Drove 40 miles to temp storage, ran pretty well. Hard to start after 1 month storage, now at home. Found EGR tube completely broken at both ends. Surprisingly the intake flange was carboned shut, sealing intake. I got one at salvage that holds moderate pressure test (mouth). During installation, it seemed short going to the EGR block. It is corrugated and I was able to stretch it aprox. 3/16 using bolts to the EGR block. I also moved the Holley thottle body to work on the intake flange bolts. The holley separated from the gasket cleanly and I nudged it all forward 1 or 2 inches. I also replaced: plugs, wires, cap, rotor, PCV, air filter. NOW - fires instantlty and idles steady at 2100. Pulling the small vacumn tube above the distribitor raises the rpm 100 - 200. Manually defelecting the EGR diapham drops the idles alot. I have checked what tubes I know of. Also unplugging the IAC control makes no change. I am on jack stands and have not driven it on the road. Before I started this it had codes 13, 14, 32, 33, and 42. During my short running time now I get no codes. My question is do I probably have a leak at the EGR tube, or while fighting the front plugs did I dislodge something I am unaware of, Or in the past has some one "adjusted" the IAC to overcome what had to be some serious running and idle issues. I have a Haynes manual<P>Thanks very much for any help. Buster<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||08-05-2000||10:15 PM||||The IAC needs to be reset if you've cleaned up everything. To reset the IAC you need to drive it over 40mph for 30 seconds to a minute. The idle should drop. Then once the car is warmed up disconnect the battery for 1 minute, hook it back up and drive normally. This will "Teach" the ECM and the car should run fine.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
